Validate a level dump or export native stage pages as JSON

Usage: vize dump [OPTIONS] <--roundtrip <FILE>|--all-levels> [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  Compile FILE (.html, .vue or .pug) and capture its executed levels

Options:
      --level <LEVEL>        L1 Vue-template source fidelity, or L2/L3 canonical Full dump bytes [possible values: l1, l2, l3]
      --roundtrip <FILE>     Read FILE and require byte identity after the selected level's roundtrip
      --all-levels           Capture only the levels executed by one product compile
      --json                 Write the stage feed as JSON
      --pipeline <PIPELINE>  Select a real product backend; named no-op passes are unsupported [possible values: dom, ssr, vapor]
      --dump-dir <DIR>       Write captured pages and the versioned product feed into DIR
      --dump-after-change    Write a page only when its bytes differ from the preceding page
      --timing-json <FILE>   Write observed timing data, including availability, as JSON
      --remarks <FILE>       Write observed remarks, including availability, as JSON
  -h, --help                 Print help
